Import "../types.clean"
Import Lean Mathlib.Topology.Basic

/-! Basic topology with explicit carrier types and topologies.
    Mathematical preimages, images, composition, and continuity are authored here.
    This first module is restricted to carrier types in Lean Type 0. -/

Type Topology(X: Type):
  Means: TopologicalSpace X
  Render latex: \operatorname{{Topology}}({X})
  Describe: a topology on ${X}$
  Describe plural: topologies on ${X}$

Notation set of(condition):
  Let X: Type
  Let condition: Function(X,Proposition)
  Returns: Set(X)
  Means: setOf condition
  Render latex: \{{x \mid {condition}(x)\}}

Condition open in(S,t):
  Let X: Type
  Let S: Set(X)
  Let t: Topology(X)
  From Lean: @IsOpen X t S
  Assumption name: openness of {S} in {t}

Define inverse image(f,S):
  Let X,Y: Type
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Let S: Set(Y)
  Returns: Set(X)
  Equals: set of(function(x: X, f(x) ∈ S))
  Render latex: {f}^{{-1}}({S})

Define image(f,S):
  Let X,Y: Type
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Let S: Set(X)
  Returns: Set(Y)
  Equals:
    set of(function(y: Y,
      there exists (x: X, x ∈ S and f(x) = y)))
  Render latex: {f}({S})

Define compose maps(g,f):
  Let X,Y,Z: Type
  Let g: Function(Y,Z)
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Returns: Function(X,Z)
  Equals: function(x: X, g(f(x)))
  Render latex: {g} \circ {f}

Condition continuous between(f,t,u):
  Let X,Y: Type
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Let t: Topology(X)
  Let u: Topology(Y)
  Holds when:
    for every (S: Set(Y),
      open in(S,u) → open in(inverse image(f,S),t))
  Assumption name: continuity of {f} from {t} to {u}
  Render: {f} is continuous from {t} to {u}

Define selected elements(S,condition):
  Let X: Type
  Let S: Set(X)
  Let condition: Function(X,Proposition)
  Returns: Set(X)
  Equals: set of(function(x: X, x ∈ S and condition(x)))

Define intersection family(sets):
  Let I,X: Type
  Let sets: Function(I,Set(X))
  Returns: Set(X)
  Equals: set of(function(x: X, for every (i: I, x ∈ sets(i))))

